 r←{noTrap}Notify(type message);body;file;icon;ps1;tag;title;⎕IO;⎕ML
⍝ Fires a Windows toast notification.\\
⍝ The toast is fired and forgotten: this function does not wait for it.
⍝ `toast.ps1`, which lives in this package's assets folder, does the actual work.\\
⍝ The caption of the notification is derived from `⎕WSID`. If that is empty or "CLEAR WS"
⍝ the last part of the current directory becomes the caption.\\
⍝ `type` and `message` must be strings, one of which might be empty:
⍝ * If `message` is not empty it is shown; `type` is ignored
⍝ * If message is empty and `type` is not, `type` is shown, followed by " is waiting for your input"
⍝ If both are empty, calling this function makes no sense.\\
⍝ The main caller is <https://github.com/aplteam/CommTools>, see there. When called by `CommTools`, `type`
⍝ is one of `YesOrNo`, `AskForNumber`, `AskForText`, `Pause`, `Select`.
⍝ `message` becomes the question, message or caption but might be empty (`Select`).\\
⍝ Returns `⍬`.
 ⎕IO←1 ⋄ ⎕ML←1   ⍝ This function might be fixed into any namespace
 noTrap←{0<⎕NC ⍵:⍎⍵ ⋄ 0}'noTrap'
 r←⍬
 :Trap (~noTrap)/0   ⍝ `CommTools` does not trap errors, and a notification must never bring an application down
     ps1←(TatinVars.GetFullPath2AssetsFolder),'/toast.ps1'
     title←⎕WSID
     :If (⊂title)∊'' 'CLEAR WS'
         title←⊃⌽'/'(≠⊆⊢)¯1↓⊃1 ⎕NPARTS''   ⍝ No workspace, so the current directory identifies the session
     :EndIf
     body←message
     :If 0=≢body
         body←type,' is waiting for your input'
     :EndIf
     body[⍸body∊⎕UCS 13 10]←' '   ⍝ A toast carries a single piece of text
     :If 200<≢body
         body←(197↑body),'...'
     :EndIf
     icon←2 ⎕NQ'.' 'GetEnvironment' 'DYALOG'
     :If 0<≢icon
         icon,←'/dyalog.exe'
     :EndIf
     file←(2 ⎕NQ'.' 'GetEnvironment' 'TEMP'),'/dyalog-notify-',(∊⍕¨⎕TS),'.txt'
     ((title body icon)'UTF-8')⎕NPUT file 1   ⍝ A nested left argument of three items would be read as (content encoding newline)
     ⍝ "Hidden" keeps the console window that `powershell.exe` is given off the screen; without it it flashes up
     {}⎕CMD('powershell.exe -NoProfile -NonInteractive -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File "',ps1,'" -From "',file,'"')'Hidden'
 :Else
     ∆NotifyError←⎕DMX   ⍝ Swallowed, but kept next to this function for diagnosis
 :EndTrap
⍝Done
